---
title: ProximaDB - Network Overview (Protocol Multiplex Flow)
---
flowchart LR
    subgraph Clients["Clients"]
        APP[App / SDK]
        BI[BI / psql]
        AGENT[Agent / LLM]
    end

    subgraph Srv5678["Unified Server :5678  (MultiServer)"]
        MUX["Multiplexer\nnetwork/multiplex/"]
        MIDDLE["Middleware\nmiddleware/tenant.rs\n(injects TenantContext)"]
        REST["REST v1+v2\nrest/v2: collections,records,\nquery,documents,entities,\ngraphs,schema,timeseries\nrest/v1: handlers,catalog,hybrid,aql"]
        GRPC["gRPC\nproto v1+v2\nrecord/graph/document/fusion service"]
        ARROW["Arrow Flight\narrow_ipc/ (zero-copy bulk)"]
    end

    subgraph Srv5433["pgwire Server :5433"]
        PGWIRE["postgres/\nprotocol.rs, session.rs,\ntranslator.rs"]
        PIPE["relational_pipeline.rs\n(SQL lowering)"]
    end

    subgraph SrvMCP["MCP Server"]
        MCP["network/mcp/\n(catalog introspection,\ndiscovery for agents)"]
    end

    APP -->|HTTP/gRPC/Flight| MUX
    BI -->|Postgres wire| PGWIRE
    AGENT -->|MCP| MCP

    MUX --> MIDDLE
    MIDDLE --> REST
    MIDDLE --> GRPC
    MIDDLE --> ARROW
    PGWIRE --> PIPE

    REST --> SVC["Services\n(services/)"]
    GRPC --> SVC
    ARROW --> SVC
    PIPE --> ROUTER["ComputeScheduler\n(query/)"]
    REST --> ROUTER

    classDef port fill:#fff8e1,stroke:#f57f17
    class MUX,PGWIRE,MCP port
